#! `$/cancelRequest` for an id that was already answered, and for one that
#! never existed. Both must be dropped silently: the protocol says a cancel
#! for an unknown id is a no-op, and clients send them routinely because the
#! response and the cancel cross on the wire. A server that errors, or that
#! keeps such ids forever, leaks a little on every keystroke.
name      cancel/cancel-unknown-id
profile   minimal

initialize
open      hello.lu
wait      diagnostics hello.lu
req       hover hello.lu 8:4
cancel    2
cancel    9999
req       documentSymbol hello.lu
shutdown
